Z||000000||Pretender||04-29-99||07:56 PM||||Ok, i went to five different parts stores(sears/autozone/advacedauto/westernauto/and pepboys) to get the star shaped socket "E-16"(size to take off the upper intake manifold star bolts)....i finally got it from the "snap-on man" that had stopped in at the garage behind my house. I think that they all have the socket but they were just "out", just thought i'd let you guys/gals know incase your planning on removing the upper-intake.. :0)<br>
Z||000001||Phil||04-30-99||05:58 AM||||I just used a 12 point box wrench and all went fine
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||09-07-1999||07:34 PM||||10mm 12point socket will do.||||reg||
Z||000003||BENGAL4||09-07-1999||09:37 PM||||You also need a 8mm 12 point socket for 2 of the bolts. I bought both of mine, 10mm & 8mm, at Autozone.||||reg||
Z||000004||Gokart||09-08-1999||02:01 AM||||Do you need to be a professional to take that off? Does it need to torqued back down exactly the way it came off?||||reg||
Z||000005||BENGAL4||09-08-1999||04:18 AM||||It's real easy to remove and to reinstall. There is a torque pattern that needs to be followed. If you have a Haynes manual, its right there in the front.||||reg||
